  "question": {
    "text": "Four monochromatic and coherent sources of light emitting waves in phase at placed on <math><mi>y</mi></math> axis at <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></math> and <math><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the intensity of wave reaching at point P far away on <math><mi>y</mi></math> axis from each of the source is almost the same and equal to <math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> , then the resultant intensity at P for <math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is <math><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> . The value of [n] is.<br />\rHere <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> is greatest integer function."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0061_817f7dd58d92.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 316px;\" /><br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math> between 1 and 3 <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mi>ϕ</mi></math> between 2 and 4 <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Intensity because of 1 and 3, 2 and 4<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msqrt><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msqrt><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br />Now phase difference between resultant of 1 and 3, 2 and 4 is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msqrt><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>×</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>6.8</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>"
  }
